PLEGMA (https://github.com/cylqcd/PLEGMA) is a software developed by the lattice QCD groups
at the University of Cyprus, The Cyprus Institute and the University of Bonn to be used
for projects within the Extended Twisted Mass Collaboration (ETMC), thereafter called the owners.
Any other group within ETMC who may wish to contribute is welcome and may be added to the list of owners.
Copying and/or distributing any files of PLEGMA can only be done notifying the developers
and filling the online license form https://forms.gle/SixDLvko6h5NLZ1i8. 
Please register new projects at https://forms.gle/ahnRxTx246r48kT97. 
You may use PLEGMA only after registering and signing the form specifying the terms of references.
A notification will be sent to you by email. You must acknowledge the owners in any publication resulting
from the usage of PLEGMA. Violation of this copyright can result in a request of termination of usage.
